INSTALLING AND SETTING UP IKEBACK FOR USE
=======================================

Please note that all instructions in this file apply to the Linux version of
Ikeback. Users of the Windows version of Ikeback should run the installer which will
guide you through the installation. Afterwards the graphical Ikeback Configurator
helps to set up Ikeback.

For further information you can also take a look at Ikeback administrator manual:

	http://docs.ikeback.io/en/latest/admin/index.html


Installing Ikeback
----------------

Requirements:

First you should download the necessary packages depending on your
Linux distribution. If there're no packages for your distribution,
try to build Ikeback yourself. See according section in README file
for details.

If there're unfulfilled requirements, your package management system (dpkg,
RPM etc.) will complain about it.


Installing:

First you have to install the necessary packages on your computer(s).
On clients you only have to install the packages ikeback:

on DPKG-based systems:

        dpkg -i  ikeback...deb

on RPM-based systems:

	rpm -i  ikeback...rpm

Of course, if your linux distribution has available such package you can install it from repositories:

	apt install ikeback

	dnf install ikeback


Essentially, there are 3 main apps in package:

-  ikeback-configurator
-  ikeback-service
-  ikeback-master


On the master computer you must be sure to have installed ikeback-master.
On clients computers remove ikeback-master if you installed it.



Setup a Ikeback client
--------------------

On clients you have to make sure that the Ikeback Service is being started when
either X is started or a user logs on. There're several methods to achieve this
(this is why it's not done automatically when installing the package):

1. Add the appropriate command ("ikeback-service &") to /etc/X11/xinit/xinitrc or
   add an according desktop file to /etc/xdg/autostart.
   This method isn't recommend, because ICA then runs with the user's
   privileges -> the user is able to kill ICA and get out of teacher's
   control.

2. add "ikeback-service &" to /etc/X11/xdm/Xsetup. On some systems, this
   doesn't take effect, so either edit /etc/kde4/kdm/Xsetup or
   /etc/X11/gdm/Xsetup

You can easily test whether all is fine by running telnet on port 11100 of the
according compter.

example:

	telnet 192.168.1.2 11100


You should see something like "RFB 003.008".


Setting up and configuring Ikeback
---------------------------------

Please refer to the official Ikeback Administrator Manual at http://docs.ikeback.io/en/latest/admin/index.html
